### extlinux .DTBO files

This folder contains .dtbo files to enable BeagleY-AI Peripheral modules.

To enable the modules, copy the files to BeagleY-AI's: /boot/firmware/overlays, 
then add the modules to your extlinux configuration (fdtoverlays <.dtbo> <.dtbo> <.dtbo>)
  

How to copy:
1. Use your NFS filesystem, copy the module you want to enable to you NFS, then on your BeagleY-AI, copy it to the overlay folder.
2. Use scp. Open this (extlinux_.dtbo) folder on your terminal, then run: 
  
  scp ./<module>.dtbo beagley@<beagley_IP-Address>:/boot/firmware/overlays

  Example:

  scp ./k3-am67a-beagley-ai-eqep0.dtbo beagley@192.168.7.2:/boot/firmware/overlays

### Contained modules in this folder:
1. k3-am67a-beagley-ai-eqep0.dtbo
  Enables AM67A EQEP(Enhanced Quadrature Encoder Pulse) Module. This modules counts the number on encoder pulses on a dedicated pin. Used for high speed & high reliability counting using a rotary encoder.

### Refer:
TI's AM67A Processors Datasheet : https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/am67a.pdf
TI's AM67 Processor Sillicon TRM: https://www.ti.com/lit/zip/SPRUJB3


